sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-marine-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-marine-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-marine-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Schnakenberg wavelength at 52 µm for the Late Pleistocene marine stickleback (Pass 1 bare field) — MorphoEval overall 72.4/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 1 reports the bare Schnakenberg activator (k_c^2 = 0.775, λ = 52 µm, age 0.015 Ma). Radial Pearson against the Holger Krisp CC BY 4.0 photograph is 0.262 and the z-scored radial RMSE is 1.215. The photograph's flank bars measure about 641 µm, which is not the 52 µm carrier. Overall 72.4/100 (faithfulness 66.9, reproducibility 85.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 1e3ee6a7276ce724ef7f1d6520314b48f92f2571; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 84, Morphological realism / specimen match 52, Parameter expressivity 74, Morphometric validation 64, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 82, Reproducibility package 84. Output judged: docs/media/gasterosteus_aculeatus_marine_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-marine-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 1e3ee6a7276ce724ef7f1d6520314b48f92f2571, image/png, 974955 B, 1344×1008 px, artifact_sha256 0cc5f613d7051cd4c73558880eddd34423bbe658e538be03fb2b1c13916852e6 (sha256 0cc5f613d7051cd4c73558880eddd34423bbe658e538be03fb2b1c13916852e6), spec_fingerprint ec8f8df9412a2bb584929165130a30cbd90307993ad2e994914eb1033f764490. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: ec8f8df9412a2bb584929165130a30cbd90307993ad2e994914eb1033f764490; artifact_sha256: 0cc5f613d7051cd4c73558880eddd34423bbe658e538be03fb2b1c13916852e6; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/gasterosteus_aculeatus_marine_turing_wavelength_s0/gasterosteus_aculeatus_marine_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=c476c5afc7fa866b..., datasets/gasterosteus_aculeatus_marine_turing_wavelength_s0/gasterosteus_aculeatus_marine_turing_wavelength_s0_specimen.jpg=0c9e2c6dfe107e95..., datasets/gasterosteus_aculeatus_marine_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=2f5f640058f3b6a0..., datasets/gasterosteus_aculeatus_marine_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=ca3ca7bbea34ab1f...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) critical wavenumber from the dispersion determinant | Colosimo et al. (2004, 2005) Eda complete-plate versus low-plate morphs | Bell, Baumgartner and Olson (1985) temporal change in G. doryssus armor characters; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg (a, b, D_u, D_v) placed so the marine wavelength is 52 µm | λ(N) = 52 µm * sqrt(32/N) giving 104 µm (doryssus_late) and 78 µm (living aculeatus); transfer_boundary: N_eff = 8 for the predecessor is the Colosimo low-morph analogy, not a Truckee plate count | The 2020 German photograph is an extant anatomical plate, not a 15 ka fossil; does_not_claim: That 52 µm was measured on a fossil melanophore | That the bare activator image is a pixel match to the photograph." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Goodness-of-fit: bare-field radial Pearson is 0.262. Fit a specimen-locked gain and recompute Pearson, RMSE, and KS.",
            "remediation needed: Negative control: equal diffusion (Du = Dv) must stay outside the Turing band and the pattern/control activator-std ratio must exceed 3.",
            "remediation needed: Parameter-regime sweep: require λ(s) to increase monotonically for s in {0.64, 1, 2.25, 4}.",
            "remediation needed: Real specimen CV segmentation: report foreground fraction, structure-tensor coherency, and flank-bar spacing, and keep bar spacing unequal to the 52 µm reference." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.724"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (single builder-assessor; no second provider on this pass)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://x.ai> .
}

